  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Output/s</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output/s as listed by the project staff.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Supply of finance for women enhanced 
Indicator: 100% of ADB FIL (PRs equivalent of USD 50 M), including recycled amounts, utilized for providing access to finance to Beneficiary Financial Institutions (MFBs, NBMFCs, and DBs) for exclusive use for women sub-loans.
It is estimated that FIL additional financing will provide 613,000 sub-loans to women. 
Data Source: SBP semiannual progress reports 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2024"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2025-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="613000"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Women entrepreneurship capacity enhanced 
Indicator: To empower women entrepreneurs and address barriers to women entrepreneurship, MOIP submits a dedicated Women Entrepreneurship Development Policy for approval of the Federal Cabinet, that includes: 
(i) clear definitions of Women Small &amp; Medium Enterprises; (ii) an Action Plan to promote women entrepreneurship (as defined in the policy); and (iii) a time bound implementation roadmap for 2025-2030. 
Data Source: MOIP submission of Women Entrepreneurship Development Policy to cabinet 
Baseline year: 2024 
Baseline value: N 
Baseline year: 2024 
Baseline value: N 
Target year: 2025 
Target value: Y</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Women representation in the financial sector strengthened 
Indicator: SBP establishes a gender sensitivity toolkit to enable the banks to refine and customize their own gender sensitivity training programs for management, staff, and sales positions to be implemented by December 2024 to support the industry implement gender sensitivity programs 
Data Source: Gender sensitivity toolkit confirmation from SBP/ notification to the industry 
Baseline year: 2024 
Baseline value: Not applicable 
Baseline year: 2024 
Baseline value: Not applicable 
Target year: 2025 
Target value: Y</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Women-centered legal and regulatory frameworks established 
Indicator: To support compliance, monitoring and supervision of the BOE policy and directives, SBP: (i) improves its supervisory tools and increased capacity to perform systematic assessments of gender service quality on its regulated entities and pilots supervisory assessments with at least 2 banks; (ii) establishes a BOE performance scorecard rating tool to monitor banks&amp;apos; achievements in (a) establishing women services departments,  (b) women centered business targets (credit, deposit, and payment services) and (c) targets for women representation in branches and branchless banking service segments, (iii) increases the scope and definition of the women SME target to commercial banks under BOE to include both retail lending to women SMEs and wholesale lending to microfinance providers targeting productive loans for micro women enterprises to count towards achievement of the target. 
Data Source: SBP reports, publication, and circulars 
Baseline year: 2024 
Baseline value: N 
Baseline year: 2024 
Baseline value: N 
Target year: 2025 
Target value: Y</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
